{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Songs From The Silver Screen connects my interest in soundtracks and musicals with the expressive singing I want to hear now.",
    "Awakening and Partners fit my interest in classical crossover, polished vocals, and melodic songs, which connects with my listening to Stages and vocal ensembles."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me and Noel connect with my past Christmas listening, but seasonal songs do not suit what I want on this visit.",
    "2015 GRAMMY Nominees offers a broad selection of hits when I want a more consistent vocal and orchestral listening experience."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past interest in Christmas recordings seems to have been treated as an ongoing desire for holiday music.",
    "My interest in melodic singing seems to have been stretched to include broad pop collections, although the vocal style and musical setting matter to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest relaxing classical selection suggests that atmosphere matters now, alongside my longer interest in expressive vocals.",
    "I am especially drawn to the connection between film or musical songs and expressive singing; a soundtrack alone or a vocal album with an unclear identity is less compelling."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in expressive singing but gave too much weight to past holiday listening and too little to the musical atmosphere I want now."
}"}
